d=Document(out/'Architectural_Economy_v5.docx'); p=d.paragraphs
# Preserve styles and untouched XML (including existing equations and figures).
p[2].text=p[2].text.replace('Version 5.0','Version 6.0')
p[7].text='An exploratory genomic pilot tested whether weakly buffered downstream influence predicts noncoding sequence constraint (H2), combining K562 perturbation profiles, ABC enhancer–gene maps and 241-way phyloP scores (636 regions, 408 genes). The association was not supported: adjusted reach β = −0.026 (95% CI −0.094 to 0.042); reach–buffering interaction β = 0.012 (−0.056 to 0.080). Held-out prediction deteriorated with added predictors. We therefore distinguish sequence constraint from a prospective hypothesis of functional continuity (H3). Functional Equivalence Mapping (H3-M) proposes measuring sequence divergence against independently assayed activity in primate enhancers, using prespecified equivalence limits, then testing whether architectural measures predict tolerance. Neither H3 nor H3-M has yet been tested here.'
p[8].text='Keywords: architectural economy; PDP-8; regulatory genomics; evolutionary constraint; functional continuity; functional equivalence; robustness.'
p[12].text=p[12].text+' A molecular entry point is the existence of alternative sequences that satisfy the same measurable functional requirements; Sections 7.2–7.3 develop a test of this proposition.'
for s in d.sections:
 for f in s.footer.paragraphs:
  for r in f.runs:
   if '(v5)' in r.text:r.text=r.text.replace('(v5)','(v6)')
anchor=p[154]
def add(t,style='Body Text',breakbefore=False):
 q=anchor.insert_paragraph_before(t,style=style)
 if breakbefore:q.paragraph_format.page_break_before=True
 return q
add('7.2 Molecular functional equivalence (H3-M)','Heading 3',True)
add('Sequence substitution and the functional contract','Heading 4')
add('The same function can be realized by more than one nucleotide sequence. In coding DNA, synonymous substitutions preserve the amino-acid sequence but may alter expression or splicing; conservative amino-acid substitutions can preserve a biochemical activity without guaranteeing identical protein function. In noncoding DNA, changes in binding sites, compensatory substitutions and enhancer turnover can preserve regulatory activity [34,35,37,39,40]. The analogy to the PDP-8 is a compatible functional interface, not an assumption that genes execute software. Molecular equivalence is always relative to a specified assay, cellular context and tolerance; it does not imply equivalence of whole organisms.')
add('We propose Functional Equivalence Mapping (FEM) to characterize this many-to-one relationship. For corresponding sequences s and t, let d(s,t) be substitutions per comparable aligned base (indels reported separately), and let Δ = A(t) − A(s), where A is measured log₂ reporter enrichment in a common experimental context. The pair satisfies the operational activity requirement when the true Δ lies between −δ and +δ, where δ is an independently justified maximum tolerable difference. Equivalence within a tolerance is a pairwise relation, not necessarily transitive. Figure 12 shows how molecular divergence and assay-level equivalence are distinguished.')
q=add('');q.alignment=WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER;q.paragraph_format.keep_with_next=True;q.add_run().add_picture(str(work/'FEM_figure12.png'),width=Inches(6.1))
q=add('Figure 12. Functional Equivalence Mapping (FEM). (A) The shaded band denotes a prespecified activity tolerance independent of sequence divergence. (B) Example interval-based decisions: a 90% confidence interval entirely within ±δ supports equivalence at a 5% two-one-sided-test level; an interval wholly beyond a margin supports a difference exceeding that margin; overlap may be inconclusive. Illustrative design, not experimental measurements [41].');q.runs[0].italic=True;q.runs[0].font.size=Pt(9)
add('H3-M: among active, comparable regulatory sequences, independently measured buffering and alternative regulatory implementations should predict activity equivalence beyond sequence divergence and conventional covariates. The prediction is conditional: extra coordinating dependencies may offset the benefit of redundancy. This is a molecular subhypothesis of H3; activity equivalence alone cannot demonstrate preservation of network coordination.')
add('7.3 Prospective research program: from sequence to coordination','Heading 3',True)
add('Study A: primate enhancer equivalence','Heading 4')
add('Klein et al. [39] assayed 11 extant primate orthologs and nine reconstructed ancestral versions of human-active enhancer tiles in HepG2 cells, obtaining activity scores for 5,426 sequences across 344 tiles. They already quantified sequence–activity divergence; FEM is not a claim of priority for this comparison. The proposed extension is explicit equivalence testing followed by held-out evaluation of architectural predictors. Supplementary Table S4 and GEO GSE113978 provide the starting resources. Whalen et al. [40] identified opposing predicted effects of substitutions in human-accelerated regions and tested regulatory activity in human and chimpanzee neural progenitor cells, providing a complementary context for evaluating candidate compensation.')
add('Freeze the sequence alignment policy, cohort, activity filters, equivalence margin, and precision criteria before testing. Use replicate-level measurements where available; barcodes are not independent biological replicates. Estimate paired activity differences with replicate-aware uncertainty, use two one-sided tests (TOST) [41], and report equivalent, meaningfully different and inconclusive pairs separately. If summary scores lack valid uncertainty, restrict the analysis to descriptive candidates. Account for related sequences and overlapping tiles using locus-level resampling and phylogenetically informed models. A high-divergence subset must be defined in advance. Report ascertainment of human-active liver candidates and uncertainty in reconstructed ancestors; neither inactive sequences nor unmeasured pairs are evidence of successful equivalence.')
add('Test candidate compensation with measured ancestral, single-substitution and combined-substitution constructs where available. Restoration toward ancestral activity supports compensation; nonadditive epistasis requires departure from an explicitly defined additive expectation. Reporter assays isolate aspects of sequence activity but do not establish endogenous target regulation. Where independent motif multiplicity, enhancer redundancy or perturbational measurements are available, compare a baseline model (divergence, activity, length, assay context and phylogeny) against a model augmented with architecture. Hold out entire enhancer loci or clades; avoid using activity outcomes to construct predictors. Treat absence of predictive improvement in a well-powered analysis as evidence against H3-M.')
add('Study B: coordination across biological systems','Heading 4')
add('The next level is comparative input–output testing. The cross-species immune-response dataset of Hagai et al. [42] supplies a prospective starting point for comparing independently defined pathway responses and activation timing under matched stimuli. Match cell populations, time points and donor-level replicates; compare module agreement to expression-, size- and detectability-matched controls and within-species reliability. Equivalent responses alone do not establish preserved causal wiring. Test matched regulator perturbations where suitable data exist, and then ask whether independently estimated architectural reach and buffering predict cross-species response continuity beyond established covariates. These are new experiments, not results of the present study.')
# Strengthen the conclusion while preserving its final line.
p[158].text='The refined research question is whether selection can preserve consequential coordination while permitting its molecular implementation to change, and whether architecture adds predictive value beyond established evolutionary models. FEM provides an operational starting point: identify different nucleotide sequences satisfying the same assay-level functional requirement, test candidate compensation, and then determine whether the resulting tolerance extends to independently measured regulatory relationships and perturbational responses. The proposed H3-M and H3 tests are not confirmation of H2. They distinguish continuity of output from continuity of internal wiring and set a falsifiable path from molecular activity to coordinated system behavior.'
p[159].paragraph_format.keep_with_next=False
p[163].text='Code and data availability: the research repository (https://github.com/RandoSY/architectural-economy) preserves earlier manuscript versions, computational benchmarks, audit materials and corrected H2 pilot results. The H3 and H3-M research agendas are available under research/. New molecular and comparative-response datasets are identified in [39,40,42]; no new H3-M or H3 analyses are reported. Archival DOI and complete v6 repository transfer are pending.'
